From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MikolajQ <mikolaj.q@wp.pl>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 20:19:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] sm6225-common: perf: Mark cpu_min_freq/cpu_max_freq
 unsupported

Our kernel (Tomoms/Sultan fork) has no msm_performance, so every perf
lock that touches /sys/module/msm_performance/parameters/cpu_{min,max}_freq
fails and logs "ANDR-PERF-RESOURCEQS: Failed to apply optimization [2, 0]".
With the LineageOS power HAL sending a scroll boost every ~250 ms of
touch, that was 300-680 error lines per minute of interaction on rhode
(13.10.2026), the top writer to the main log buffer. Declare both
resources unsupported, as the file's own notes suggest, so the perf HAL
skips them quietly. No behaviour change: the writes never succeeded.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Dr8X39PngEfThUaxTxyj9B
---
 proprietary/vendor/etc/perf/targetresourceconfigs.xml | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/proprietary/vendor/etc/perf/targetresourceconfigs.xml b/proprietary/vendor/etc/perf/targetresourceconfigs.xml
index 0180b1d..09ac543 100644
--- a/proprietary/vendor/etc/perf/targetresourceconfigs.xml
+++ b/proprietary/vendor/etc/perf/targetresourceconfigs.xml
@@ -26,6 +26,9 @@ as anyway perflock calls of these resources would fail. -->
 
         <Config MajorValue="0x1" MinorValue="0x2" Node="/proc/sys/kernel/sched_busy_hyst_ns" />
 
+        <Config MajorValue="0x2" MinorValue="0x0" Supported="no" /> <!-- cpu_min_freq: no msm_performance in our kernel -->
+        <Config MajorValue="0x2" MinorValue="0x1" Supported="no" /> <!-- cpu_max_freq: no msm_performance in our kernel -->
+
         <Config MajorValue="0x3" MinorValue="0x3" Supported="no" /> <!-- sched_small_task -->
         <Config MajorValue="0x3" MinorValue="0x6" Supported="no" /> <!-- sched_init_task_load -->
         <Config MajorValue="0x3" MinorValue="0xA" Supported="no" /> <!-- sched_add_group -->
